#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:5
#: 238b7361cd2b4bf493b8aeff054eff8d
msgid "Motor Thrust Scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:7
#: d764736410ab48f391f016ba1174a087
msgid ""
"Copter includes *motor thrust scaling* which compensates for the non-"
"linear thrust output of most ESCs and motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:12
#: 15f16c0b18ce4c899d3323f7bac3f449
msgid ""
"The default curve should work for nearly all ESC/motor combinations. "
"Normally the parameters should not be adjusted unless the vehicle’s "
"actual thrust curve has been measured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:17
#: a158a14669db4db2845b0f58e9110dc7
msgid "Thrust Curves"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:19
#: 7e4fa0b5cf9f490ca719803012115717
msgid "The curve is controlled by two parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:21
#: f4264b36183546bf8c7d1e8663926ca1
msgid ""
":ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO<MOT_THST_EXPO>` controls the shape of the thrust "
"curve with \"0\" meaning a completely linear curve and \"1.0\" being very"
" curved (see pictures below).  The default is \"0.65\" (the image below "
"incorrectly states the default is 0.5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:26
#: 78819570b260480c8b6496385903ac55
msgid ""
"Some ESCs have built-in linearizing curves and the default EXPO value of "
"\"0.65\" will cause stability issues, requiring thrust stand measurements"
" to adjust the EXPO. Typically, values of \"0\" to \"0.2\" will result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:31
#: 90b8c8d076fd43e48787343aa3165acc
#, python-format
msgid ""
":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MAX<MOT_SPIN_MAX>` controls the point at which the thrust "
"flattens out near its maximum.  By default this is 0.95 meaning 95% of "
"full throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:36
#: 469b23194d6744e5a90d03d25fb91775
msgid "Thrust Stands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:38
#: 0252d40ccb6646f7a777dfddf68d94d5
msgid ""
"The thrust stands listed below can be used to measure the PWM signal vs "
"thrust output for a vehicle's specific motor, esc and battery. Be sure to"
" use the ESCs rated input PWM range when measuring these values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:40
#: defe3afe2d454c65bb855055a5b17587
msgid ""
"`RCbenchmark.com thrust stands "
"<https://www.rcbenchmark.com/pages/series-1580-thrust-stand-"
"dynamometer>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:41
#: b9ef32dcd1b84b3ea9ce181f892d26e1
msgid ""
"`Turnigy thrust stand <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-thrust-stand-"
"and-power-analyser-v3.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:44
#: fe52e47981744abe8c8feafe78c81bd6
msgid "Parameter Calculation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/motor-thrust-scaling.rst:46
#: 6d3197db55924b1bab5f08fc0672f9a8
msgid ""
"A copy of `this spreadsheet "
"<https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_75aZqiT_K1CdduhUe4-DjRgx3Alun4p8V2pt6vM5P8/edit#gid=0>`__"
" can be used to calculate the appropriate values from the thrust stand "
"data above."
msgstr ""

